{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The heavens.</b> Rabbi Moses said: the heavens are like a place. And I have already explained it in Sefer HaShem, that שמים follows the pattern of a dual and is derived from שם, on account of two places fixed in the foundation, which are planted. So too it is written: \"to plant שמים and to found earth\" (Isaiah 51:16). And those lacking understanding thought that human dominion over the earth is like HaShem's dominion over the heavens, and they did not speak correctly, for HaShem's kingdom rules over all — He merely gave an explanation to human beings: that man is like Elohim's appointed officer on earth, over everything that is in it, and all is by the word of HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 115, :notes {0 "Reading והכל בדבר השם as a concluding clause; the syntax of the final sentence is compressed and the division between רק פירוש נתן לבני האדם and the following gloss is ambiguous in the witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:46.937441958Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}